    <statement><p>Match the planar vector field <m>\mathbf{F} = \left\lt  3 x + 3, y\right&gt;</m> with
the corresponding plot in the Figures below.</p>
<image xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" pi:generated="webwork/images/Library__WHFreeman__Rogawski_Calculus_Early_Transcendentals_Second_Edition__16_Line_and_Surface_Integrals__16_1_Vector_Fields__16_1_15_pg-image-1.png" width="32%"/>
<p><m>\Leftarrow</m> <alert>Plot 1</alert> <m>\quad</m></p>
<image xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" pi:generated="webwork/images/Library__WHFreeman__Rogawski_Calculus_Early_Transcendentals_Second_Edition__16_Line_and_Surface_Integrals__16_1_Vector_Fields__16_1_15_pg-image-2.png" width="32%"/>
<p><m>\Leftarrow</m> <alert>Plot 2</alert></p>
